ss":"collecting"},{"surface":"பிண்டம்","parts":[{"text":"பிண்டம்","lemma":"piṇṭam","gloss":"tax"}],"gloss":"tax"},{"surface":"நச்சின்","parts":[{"text":"நச்சின்","lemma":"nacciṉ","gloss":"if he desires"}],"gloss":"if he desires"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"yāṉai","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"புக்க","parts":[{"text":"புக்க","lemma":"puku","gloss":"that entered"}],"gloss":"that entered"},{"surface":"புலம்","parts":[{"text":"புலம்","lemma":"pulam","gloss":"field"}],"gloss":"field"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"pōla","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தானும்","parts":[{"text":"தானும்","lemma":"tāṉ","gloss":"himself"}],"gloss":"himself"},{"surface":"உண்ணான்","parts":[{"text":"உண்ணான்","lemma":"uṇ","gloss":"will not eat"}],"gloss":"will not eat"},{"surface":"உலகமும்","parts":[{"text":"உலகமும்","lemma":"ulakam","gloss":"the world too"}],"gloss":"the world too"},{"surface":"கெடுமே","parts":[{"text":"கெடுமே","lemma":"keṭu","gloss":"will be ruined"}],"gloss":"will be ruined"}]}],"literal":"If one harvests ripe grain and feeds it in mouthfuls / even less than a 'ma' of land will last for many days. / Even if it is a hundred fields, if the elephant enters alone and eats / what is ruined by its feet is much greater than what enters its mouth. / If a wise king knows the proper way and taxes / he will accumulate crores and the country will greatly flourish. / If he is a weak ruler and every day / with a clamorous retinue that does not know merit / desires taxes collected so that love perishes / like the field entered by an elephant / he himself will not eat, and the world too will be ruined.","translation":"If one harvests ripe grain and feeds it in mouthfuls, even a small plot of land, less than a 'ma', will last for many days. But even if there are a hundred fields, if an elephant enters them alone to feed, what it tramples and destroys with its feet is far greater than what enters its mouth. If a wise king knows the proper way and taxes his people gently, he will amass millions and his country will greatly flourish. But if he is a weak ruler, surrounded by a clamorous retinue that does not understand merit, and greedily demands heavy taxes till love perishes, then, like the field entered by that elephant, he himself will not enjoy the wealth, and his entire world will be ruined.","modern":"விளைந்த நெல்லை அறுத்து உணவுக் கவளங்களாக உருட்டி யானைக்குக் கொடுத்தால், ஒரு மாவிற்கும் குறைவான நிலத்தில் விளைந்த நெல்லும் பல நாட்களுக்கு உணவாகும். ஆனால், நூறு வயல்களாக இருந்தாலும், யானை தானே தனியாகப் புகுந்து தின்றால், அதன் வாய்க்குள் செல்வதை விட அதன் கால்களால் மிதிபட்டு அழியும் நெல் மிக அதிகமாகும். அறிவுடைய அரசன் வரி வாங்கும் முறையை அறிந்து வரி வசூலித்தால், கோடி கோடியாகச் செல்வம் சேர்ந்து நாடு மிகவும் செழிக்கும். ஆனால், அவன் மென்மையான அறிவுடையவனாய், தகுதி அறியாத ஆரவாரச் சுற்றத்தாரோடு சேர்ந்து, மக்களின் அன்பு கெடுமாறு வரியைக் கொடுமையாகத் திரட்ட விரும்பினால், யானை புகுந்த வயலைப் போல, அரசனும் உண்ண மாட்டான், நாடும் கெட்டுப் போகும்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai and the Ceviyaṟivuṟūu tuṟai, where a poet offers advice and counsel to a ruler. The poet Pisiranthaiyar addresses the Pandyan king Arivudai Nambi, advising him on the righteous way to collect taxes from his subjects. He uses a vivid agricultural metaphor: if grain is harvested and fed to an elephant in small, prepared portions, even a tiny plot of land can sustain it for a long time. However, if the elephant is allowed to roam freely in a vast field, it will trample and waste far more food than it actually consumes. Similarly, a wise king who taxes his people moderately and systematically will ensure prosperity for both the state and the citizens. Conversely, an oppressive ruler who demands excessive taxes through an ignorant retinue will ruin the economy, leaving nothing for himself or his people.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,1.0],[1.0,1.4],[1.